&lt;p&gt;Time Off and Work-Life Balance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days annual leave plus bank holidays, and company sick pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Support and Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest-free loan for rail season tickets &amp;amp; further education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised bicycle purchase through Cycle to Work scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Professional Development and Recognition&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous professional and personal development support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee recognition and reward programs to mark achievements and milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Community and Impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to volunteer, donate, and participate in community give-back initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to have a significant impact on your team and the business in the work that you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently exceed revenue targets through strategic sales and account management efforts, aligning with broader commercial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate relationships in managed accounts, aiming to elevate them to the Regional/Enterprise level or identify opportunities for MSAs across the global portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new revenue growth by capitalizing on opportunities in the experiential events market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a go-to expert on Convene product offerings, including meetings and technology solutions, and translate product features into functional client solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an engaging sales presence, both in person and virtually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate thorough knowledge of competitors, articulating the Convene story and differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow demand through strategic account development, expanding your network of contacts, and building long-term relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date knowledge of Convene products and locations, contributing to local and regional brand building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the local, regional, and global business plan to ensure personal targets align with overall sales objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market intelligence and industry trends with the Senior Leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and coordinate site inspections, virtual tours, client meetings, and quarterly business reviews for key accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discover and build relationships with new decision-makers, while nurturing current and prospective clients and referral partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond rapidly to client inquiries and maintain up-to-date account details for key accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and close agreements, adhering to internal pricing guidelines while ensuring client specifications are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed of competitive landscape and maintain relationships with industry counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend trade shows, networking sessions, and events to prospect for new business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed budgeted financial goals for both quarterly and annual targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate relationships with allocated key accounts through consultative sales efforts to achieve and surpass commercial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage a portfolio of accounts based on location, volume, and spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Target and secure new business to increase market share across the global portfolio of brands and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure repeat business from allocated accounts, ensuring long-term client satisfaction and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a commercial role within the UK meetings and events industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in selling to London’s corporate and agency markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of experiential events across business and consumer markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional networking abilities and relationship-building sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable of working independently while thriving in a team-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CD1&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead AI Enablement Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Belfast&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department: &lt;/strong&gt;Engineering Enablement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; VP Enablement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Full time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About EverQuote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EverQuote’s vision is to make it more efficient to shop for and buy insurance with confidence. We use data, technology and marketplace expertise to connect insurance shoppers with providers and help our customers grow their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As AI becomes part of everyday work across the organisation, we want every colleague, technical or not, to get real value from it. Our enablement teams make that possible by turning new AI capabilities into reliable, trusted services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lead AI Enablement Engineer sits within Engineering Enablement and owns the integration, usability and adoption of EverQuote’s enterprise AI services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also partner with IT, Security and Platform Engineering on service support and controls, and with data owners on access, privacy and auditability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help everyone across our organisation get more value from AI. We are looking for a hands-on Lead AI Enablement Engineer to make our AI products and services connected, reliable and useful in everyday work across Finance, Operations, HR, Sales, Engineering and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We already use Claude, and there is significant opportunity to improve the experience through relevant features, connectors, skills and access to trusted knowledge. You will turn that opportunity into working services and practical ways of working that colleagues adopt and value, while evolving our capabilities as AI technology advances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the technical integration and continuous improvement of these services, combining engineering depth with curiosity about LLMs and a strong customer focus. The role combines hands-on delivery with technical leadership and mentoring.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will shape how an entire organisation works with AI. You will have the opportunity to explore new capabilities, turn promising ideas into dependable services and see the impact directly in colleagues’ daily work. Your technical decisions and customer insight will help define a new AI capability and how it evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Own the AI service roadmap:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how colleagues work and identify friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise improvements with department leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat technical and non-technical employees as customers, and test changes with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate AI into everyday work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and administer enterprise AI products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other enablement teams to make sure the tooling is fully integrated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with InfoSec to make sure risks and standards have been met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build connectors, MCP integrations, APIs and lightweight services that connect approved tools, business systems and knowledge sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep permissions and data access aligned with users’ existing entitlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn new capabilities into useful services&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track model releases, product features and emerging tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate quality, usability, cost and risk against real tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend, pilot and roll out improvements with clear guidance and a way to reverse unsuccessful changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create reusable capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make skills, shared instructions, workflow templates and agents discoverable, with clear owners, testing and version control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams adapt proven approaches to their own work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Show colleagues what is possible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run practical demonstrations, workshops, office hours and hands-on sessions using real business workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a network of departmental champions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make guidance accessible to different confidence and skill levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the end-user experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor integration health, answer quality and user feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate failures and recurring friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate fixes, vendor escalations, change communications and support arrangements with IT, Security and Platform Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide technical leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish integration and evaluation standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor others and shape vendor decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously keep up to date with the latest LLM releases and harnesses to better inform the direction of the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security and data owners on access, privacy, auditability and safe tool use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 years experience in software development with 3+ years in AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on engineering experience building and supporting integrations, internal tools or enterprise services: you write maintainable code, work with APIs and authentication, and diagnose problems across connected systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience applying LLMs and AI tools to real workflows used by other people, with an understanding of context, retrieval, tool use and evaluation, the limits of model outputs, and when human review is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sustained interest in AI tooling, demonstrated through experimentation and working solutions. You follow developments actively and can explain which changes are worth adopting, which need more testing and which add little value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-focused approach: you listen, observe how work happens and stay involved until the solution is useful. You can support a non-technical colleague and discuss integration trade-offs with an engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of technical leadership, prioritisation and cross-functional delivery: you can turn broad needs into a practical roadmap, set standards and bring others with you through coaching and clear communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering reliable services with appropriate access controls, testing, monitoring and documentation, and taking ownership of how a capability performs after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You do not need experience with every product or tool listed, but experience in several would be valuable:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claude Enterprise or similar enterprise AI products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MCP, reusable skills and agent workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise search and knowledge integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python or TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS administration, SSO and OAuth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI adoption programmes and communities of practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You put customers first: &lt;/strong&gt;You observe how work actually happens, test changes with the people who will use them and stay involved until the solution is useful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are evidence-led: &lt;/strong&gt;You evaluate new capabilities against real tasks, establish baselines with users and use evidence to improve or retire capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You stay curious: &lt;/strong&gt;You experiment, follow developments in AI and separate changes worth adopting from those that add little value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You own the outcome: &lt;/strong&gt;You take responsibility for how a capability performs after launch, not only for getting it live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You bring others with you:&lt;/strong&gt; You mentor, set standards and communicate clearly with technical and non-technical colleagues, with departmental champions and with vendors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first 90 days, you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assessed our current AI services, feature availability, integration gaps and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agreed a prioritised roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivered a small set of valuable integrations and reusable workflows across several departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established practical enablement sessions and a feedback loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, success means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustained adoption across business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Better user satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable improvements in task time or output quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will establish baselines with users, track cost alongside benefit, and use evidence to improve or retire capabilities. Feature launches and licence activation alone are not measures of success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At EverQuote, how we achieve results matters as much as the results themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Tenacious: &lt;/strong&gt;We aim high, move quickly and persist through difficult technical and organisational problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help Customers Win: &lt;/strong&gt;We prioritise work that creates meaningful and sustainable value for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Follow the Data: &lt;/strong&gt;We use evidence to guide decisions and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Our Team: &lt;/strong&gt;We communicate directly, share knowledge and leave teams and systems stronger than we found them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EverQuote is committed to equal opportunity employment and to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and consider qualified candidates without regard to characteristics protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Adjustments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to ensuring an inclusive and accessible recruitment process for all candidates. If you require any reasonable adjustments or accommodations at any stage of the interview process, please let us know and we will work with you to arrange them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;or more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=6XmzUHfuQ-i5S31_qCIpcQCQtcZ6e1ZCg-K9ZDUrOSjhU2y_ydujWqUSk1qbf0g08qVEJgBQCRrYN_rQ6s8R1bQPdaN9iF-VnAt04umDr2dE8nvrwxpZdkrAXEGT1B1W&quot;&gt;https://investors.everquote.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=77BAgL1nVeMykQsQieJyMOhYF-A1vLMHTvEuCfBOEZ3y8__JO9djvQmh39yBJX6yJu8z7nHYbHDvvyVkE2tBDSmNhEC7b1rXdBhuOD6_EEW4-W-Bal3QIK35pntX1W7wpCEWJkz5Ouui49uO507CTSlujcntR_vtPWE-rgBZ5E-p2PqAuo57e5Qv4Tv6QhC-n6qQjfy6QyTWRFcSaZnBetOgWYZADxcw-o4FsA_59RFz1Jt7fklOmQ8TWFMdjowUuoeYy-eog8rwjsES_lJwEPPqVjfaCHv76iX7KX3pOhGVuO1kDfKFQNaGgpnnqIY3W8mYzPeMJEisnZ6PgV4sgO1EVe7cY0cS8JDoOc9JMsBma3kScg5NSRPdt1ZNQvAnsjfWLaj8Q0Xmg9vqEkXqhvPvYuXbpSBpuADuxOKh8Yn2rAJzPdDDRbBgVEuYzlbVwrHM27mDXBGESKq_dfkYajMWrNGjbF3dg4omuuCvDpneGp3mrnk6IMTmwiogaLCXrp6dHSw_rVHsXixipTUhAXy7Gd_5_zeuDewZ1X_4gSV-f-fuipPZ42u2YD6RiUF-mP4WAjF7yUJkbh0nMJjY0g==&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a Staff Software Engineer with experience building large-scale software applications and distributed systems. In this role, you will help shape the technical direction for DEMS, a mission-critical product area where reliability, security, and usability matter deeply. You will collaborate with other senior and staff engineers, engineering managers, product managers, and designers to solve complex customer problems and build durable systems that scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your strong system design skills allow you to take a holistic view of architecture, reliability, and developer productivity. You raise the bar not just through your own contributions, but by reviewing designs, mentoring engineers, improving technical decision-making, and helping teams align around pragmatic, high-quality solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a senior technical contributor, you are energized by solving hard problems, reducing ambiguity, and building systems that perform under real-world demands. As a technical leader, you partner with engineering leadership on long-term technical strategy while balancing business priorities, roadmap commitments, and engineering health.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Come work in an environment where your experience, judgment, and technical leadership will directly contribute to products that help deliver better outcomes in public safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This role is based out of our London office and follows a hybrid schedule. We rely on in-person collaboration and ask that team members work onsite Tuesdays through Fridays, with the flexibility to work remotely on Mondays, unless there is an approved workplace accommodation. We believe that connection fuels innovation, and our in-office culture is designed to foster meaningful teamwork, mentorship, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high technical bar through architecture leadership, deep technical insight, and thoughtful design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical direction across one or more DEMS domains, ensuring solutions are scalable, maintainable, secure, and resilient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Engineering, Product, Design, and adjacent teams to solve some of the most important and ambiguous technical challenges in the DEMS space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and evolution of backend services, APIs, data flows, and system integrations that support mission-critical workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic risks and opportunities, and drive improvements in reliability, observability, performance, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across teams and help grow future technical leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering effectiveness by introducing better patterns, simplifying complexity, and supporting high-quality execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to implementation where needed, especially in high-leverage or high-risk areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling complex software products in a collaborative team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in backend systems and distributed system design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with cloud platforms and production service operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical solutions across multiple teams or broad product areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of system design, reliability, performance, observability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational and/or NoSQL databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of writing clean, maintainable, production-grade code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence technical direction and organizational outcomes without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly Valued&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in enterprise SaaS, mission-critical systems, compliance-sensitive domains, or workflow-heavy platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with evidence management, records systems, chain-of-custody concepts, or highly trusted data systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hybrid, on-prem, or cloud-connected product architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with languages and platforms commonly used in modern backend environments such as Java, Go, C#, Python, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits that benefit you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary and RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive pension plan with matching contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private health insurance &amp;amp; cash plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 days paid holiday + UK public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity/paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GymPass subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance &amp;amp; income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth support and wellness resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? That&#39;s ok. At Axon, we Aim Far. We think big with a long-term view because we want to reinvent the world to be a safer, better place. We are also committed to building diverse teams that reflect the communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they check every box in the job description. If you’re excited about this role and our mission to Protect Life but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification listed here, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above job description is not intended as, nor should it be construed as, exhaustive of all duties, responsibilities, skills, efforts, or working conditions associated with this job. The job description may change or be supplemented at any time in accordance with business needs and conditions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Some roles may also require legal eligibility to work in a firearms environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
