&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Autonomous Drone Software Engineer to join a swarming programme. As an engineer on a lean, high-impact team, you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not be siloed; this role spans the entire autonomy lifecycle, from developing autonomy capabilities to investigating real-world flight-test data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across the autonomy stack and partner integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with hardware engineers, product managers, and external partners to define system requirements and translate them into robust software architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust distributed state machines, leader election protocols, and fault-tolerant architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code while confidently managing complex concurrency and contention scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run rigorous tests utilizing SITL/HITL simulation environments to validate code prior to physical deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and technical documentation to elevate the team&#39;s engineering standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act decisively during flight-test investigations, applying strong engineering judgment to physical failure modes and release safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional engineering experience in robotics, embedded systems, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in modern C++, with practical experience designing, reasoning about, and debugging highly concurrent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded systems experience working close to hardware on real-time or safety-critical platforms (e.g., avionics, automotive, robotics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural understanding of distributed systems, with the ability to deliberately evaluate and select consensus designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with robust release management, versioned artifacts, and pinned dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, MAVLink, and related drone software ecosystems is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ledgy, we’re on a mission to make Europe a powerhouse of entrepreneurship by building a modern, tech-driven equity management and financial reporting platform for private and public companies. In 2026, we aim to be the leading provider for European IPOs and reporting for share-based payments. We are a value-based company with a core focus on being humble, transparent, ambitious and impactful, all in order to delivery the best experience for our customers and end users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to partner with some of the world’s leading investors. New Enterprise Associates led our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2022/09/21/ledgy-a-carta-for-european-startups-to-manage-equity-and-cap-tables-raises-22m-from-nea-sequoia-and-more/&quot;&gt;$22m Series B&lt;/a&gt; round in 2022, with Philip Chopin joining Sequoia’s Luciana Lixandru on our board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were founded in Switzerland in 2017 and today we operate globally from offices in Zurich and London. We encourage diversity and are an international team coming from 26 different countries and speaking 25 different languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer on our AI Systems team, you&#39;ll build the AI foundations and product experiences of Ledgy: the Ledgy Agent, the tools and skills it runs on, our MCP server, and the platform capabilities that let other teams embed AI safely in their domains. You&#39;ll collaborate with fellow engineers, product managers, and designers in a new and fast-moving product area where correctness matters as much as speed - our customers need equity data they can trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire remotely across the UK, Spain, Germany, Poland, and Romania. For candidates based in London, we use a hybrid model with 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team you&#39;ll join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI Systems - Develops Ledgy&#39;s AI foundations and product experiences, from AI agents and AI-assisted workflows to the platform capabilities that help other teams embed AI safely in their domains. The team works in a new and evolving product area, balancing rapid iteration with reliable execution, evaluation tooling, and responsible automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help build the future of how companies manage equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy Agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system behind our in-app agent, so equity administrators can do through AI what they do manually in the app today. Ledgy Agent takes real actions and runs real analysis on live equity data, like onboarding a stakeholder end to end, and administrators depend on its accuracy and observability. You&#39;ll design the tools, skills, context, and orchestration behind it, and how it decides to handle each request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy MCP.&lt;/strong&gt; Not everyone wants to open Ledgy to get things done. Our MCP server lets customers bring equity into the AI agents and tools they already use. You&#39;ll shape it alongside the in-app agent, so a capability built once works in both places, and you&#39;ll decide what we expose and how we keep it safe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measuring and improving the agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system we use to measure the agent&#39;s quality and learn from how customers use it: evaluations, tracing, and feedback from real conversations. You decide what &quot;good&quot; means for customers, how we measure it, and how what we learn changes what we build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling.&lt;/strong&gt; The Ledgy web application, the agent, MCP, and surfaces we haven&#39;t built yet all need the same capabilities. You&#39;ll design the foundations that let us build AI features once and reuse them everywhere, and that let other teams add AI to their domains without compromising correctness. You&#39;ll also design how it runs as usage grows: the backend infrastructure, cost, and latency behind the agent and MCP, and how we keep them reliable and observable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own real parts of this and have a say in where we invest. You&#39;ll also spend time with customers to see how administrators actually use the agent, and use that to decide what to build next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll Thrive in This Role If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t worry if you don&#39;t tick every box. These are the things that would make you an especially good fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience working as a Software Engineer, with strong TypeScript/Node fundamentals across back end and front end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped agentic or LLM-based software to production, such as an agent, an assistant, or a chat product, and you&#39;ve been the one running it. You&#39;ve debugged failures in real conversations and kept cost and latency in check as usage and models changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve designed the agent itself: tools and skills, context and prompt engineering, state, streaming, and the agent loop. You know at least one agent framework or runtime well and can say where it works and where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You improve these systems with evidence. Evals, regression sets, tracing, and feedback from real usage tell you whether a change helped, and you use them to decide what to do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep up with what the foundation labs and the wider community are learning about building agents. You try new techniques early and judge which ones make our product better and are worth adopting now, and which should wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take part in deciding what we build. You read the data, talk to customers, and push for what you think matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in a TypeScript monorepo: React and Tailwind on the front end, tRPC, Node.js, MongoDB, and Temporal on the back end. It runs on GCP with Kubernetes, managed through Terraform. The agent is currently built on the Vercel AI SDK, and we run an MCP server alongside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to know all of it, but hands-on experience building with LLMs is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Your Journey Could Look Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First day:&lt;/strong&gt; Get the app running locally and make your first commit. Your onboarding buddy helps you get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First week:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the engineers, product managers, and designers you&#39;ll work with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the agent end to end: its tools, skills, MCP surface, and how we evaluate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship a few smaller features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First month:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the wider engineering team and learn how Ledgy works and how customers use it today. This is the background you&#39;ll use for decisions later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make larger contributions and take a bigger part in code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive part of a larger piece of work, such as process, tooling, a new product, or new functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and Design to prove and deepen the value AI adds to the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in architecture and long-term decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;After the first 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a bigger role in shaping where the team is heading. Own key parts of our AI platform and decide where we can add the most value for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and raise the bar. Help teams across Ledgy add AI to what they build, whether that means advising, reviewing, or working alongside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Ledgy&#39;s technical direction, for AI and for everything else we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting to know you (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Meet with someone from our people team to talk about your experience and to ask questions about the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Coding (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; An equity domain problem to solve collaboratively using your preferred language and IDE. We want to see how you think, so this step does not allow AI. But you can freely look up syntax questions if you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Design (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A system design session where you will design an architecture for a problem from the Ledgy domain using a visual tool of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Answer behavioural style questions about your experience, using the STAR method - with a PM and EM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Interview:&lt;/strong&gt; A chance to meet one of our founders and your hiring manager for a 30-minute chat about Ledgy&#39;s mission and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer&lt;/strong&gt; 🎉&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being part of Ledgy means:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge and re-energize with flexible working hours, 25 days of vacation, and up to 40 days of remote work from outside your home country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make space for your own professional development, with a generous yearly learning &amp;amp; development budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will receive a competitive salary + benefits + equity. All salaries are aligned with competitively benchmarked ranges based on work location and levelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For candidates based in London we use a hybrid work model of 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are the platform turning browsing into shopping&lt;/strong&gt;. We connect 200 million shoppers with deals they love while boosting local sales for hundreds of top retailers and brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help consumers save time and money while making smart shopping decisions, and we support retailers and brands in engaging customers from online research to in-store purchases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2024, Shopfully joined forces with the North American company &lt;a href=&quot;https://corp.flipp.com/&quot;&gt;Flipp&lt;/a&gt;, creating a global leader in the sector. Together, we reach 400 million households and serve over 1,000 top retailers and brands across 27 markets, including Europe, Canada, the USA, Latin America, and Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;spark&lt;/strong&gt; your growth with us?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE LOOK FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🦄&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flipp + Shopfully’s Product team focuses on driving adoption and revenue of our products by identifying the biggest market opportunities, building the case for investing in them, and shipping solutions with engineering, all while representing the voice of our merchant customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Product Manager is a senior, commercially minded product leader who already understands digital advertising. This role requires a strong strategic thinker with good business sense and solid hands-on product skills who leads opportunity identification, builds decision-ready business cases, and works with engineering to ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Sales, Engineering, Data, and Marketing teams across markets to align on key business objectives. By combining market insight, customer feedback, and industry trends, you will make sure our products resonate with merchants and drive growth. We’re looking for someone who can ramp up quickly and contribute independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO &lt;/strong&gt;🏄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Understanding and Opportunity Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Marketing, Sales Engineering and customer-facing teams to understand customer needs and prioritize the opportunities that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find the highest-leverage areas to invest in, and weigh customer demand against our resources, capabilities and strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex questions into clear priorities. For example: how do we create more value for retail partners as their strategies move toward e-commerce? How do we find and build opportunities at scale as products launch in new markets?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Cases and Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases that size opportunities, weigh revenue trade-offs, and structure a clear recommendation so leadership can make a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your recommendations, and be ready to explain them and adapt them as you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy for how our products differentiate from competitors in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Finance on pricing and monetization so our offering stays cohesive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Discovery and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with merchants, advertisers, and internal teams to define problems worth solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise ruthlessly, balancing revenue impact, effort, and strategic fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with engineering to define requirements and ship, from alpha and testing through broad launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Marketing on launch timing and readiness, and run retrospectives on past launches to improve future ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignment and Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate cross-functional alignment (Engineering, Data, Sales, Marketing, Content) with a shared focus on goals and timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across markets and levels of seniority, including senior leadership, with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track progress and impact of product initiatives and communicate results clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with industry analysts, partners, and customers, and represent Flipp + Shopfully at conferences and industry events where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL NEED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;🪄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital advertising foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; supply vs. demand, how exchanges, SSPs, and DSPs work, programmatic bidding, pricing models (CPM, CPC, CPV), and fill rate and yield. Ideally gained in ad tech, a retail media network, a publisher, or a marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building business cases: sizing opportunities, weighing revenue trade-offs, and structuring recommendations for decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy: you figure things out, own the outcome and don’t need close management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine excitement about using AI tools and rethinking how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on product skills: discovery, prioritisation, and working with engineering to ship, not only strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management, with the confidence to work across markets and levels of seniority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scrappy, curious and confident approach. You’re hungry to make an impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 At our company, we value diversity and actively encourage it — we believe a variety of perspectives and backgrounds makes us stronger. We focus on potential rather than on having a “perfect” CV. If this role excites you and you believe you could grow into it — even if you don’t tick every single box in the requirements — we’d love to hear from you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎆&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail, CPG, or retail media background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-market experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can speak Italian or German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION 🌐&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have offices in Milan, Berlin, Barcelona, you can benefit from our flexible hybrid model (full remote available), empowering you to work where you&#39;re most effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOURS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;⏰&lt;br&gt;Your manager and several partner teams are in North America, so you’ll need to be flexible about working some later hours, beyond a standard 9-5 CET.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL FIND AT SHOPFULLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🤗&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 An opportunity to thrive in a rapidly scaling multinational company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕶️ A vibrant, informal, and inclusive work environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We champion autonomy, flexibility, and a hybrid work model, empowering you to own your work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 Access to learning opportunities and regular feedback sessions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍓 Enjoy our central, modern offices featuring fresh snacks, coffee (including vegan options!), and ergonomic setups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 Engage in meaningful team events: offsites, happy hours, company parties and celebrations that unite us beyond daily tasks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻We provide all the necessary equipment for you to work effectively and set up your workspace, wherever you are&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧰 Benefit from additional country-specific advantages based on local contracts and practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE &lt;/strong&gt;💜&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of 450 people (and counting!), from 30 different nationalities. We’re on a mission to innovate, and we believe the key to that is seeing the world through a variety of perspectives. That’s why building a more diverse team, as well as bringing in even more talent, is so important for us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TO FEEL AT HOME 🛋️ IN SHOPFULLY YOU NEED 🎯&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progress Over Perfection&lt;/strong&gt;: We move forward. Always. In a fast-moving world, speed with purpose beats certainty without action. Momentum matters—not for its own sake, but because it drives results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity Through Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;: We bring each other along. We work in teams, not silos. Transparency gives context, and context enables action. That means we share decisions early, publish work in progress, and document outcomes so others can learn, move faster, and build better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn Loudly&lt;/strong&gt;: We grow by doing and by daring. Big bets unlock big breakthroughs. But real innovation demands risk, and risk always carries the possibility of failure. That’s not a flaw. It’s the price of ambition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenge with Empathy&lt;/strong&gt;: We speak up, even when it’s hard—because candor shows care, and leads to better outcomes. Listening deeply is how we grow. Disagreeing openly is how we build trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always Build Better: We are builders—of products, systems, and ideas. But more than that, we are builders of better. Better has no finish line. It’s a mindset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you choose to apply for this specific job position and submit your application, which may include personal data such as your identifying details, contact information, curriculum vitae, cover letter, professional qualifications, and/or employment history, please be informed that your data may be shared with our Affiliates*, including Offerista Group GmbH and Flipp Operations Inc. The aforementioned entities will act as joint controllers for the limited purpose of intra-group sharing related to the evaluation of candidates’ applications. This means that your data may be processed by the Affiliate to assess your application and, if deemed suitable, to contact you regarding potential employment opportunities. However, please note that from the moment an Affiliate initiates direct contact with you and engages in any further processing of your personal data beyond the initial intra-group sharing for evaluation purposes, such Affiliate shall act as an independent data controller. In such cases, the processing of your personal data will be subject to the specific privacy policies that can be found&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://shopfully.com/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;* Affiliates shall mean any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by or is under common control with ShopFully SpA and its Affiliates’ subsidiaries, meaning any entity which is directly or indirectly controlled by the Affiliates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Support You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Total Rewards philosophy is to ensure that you are rewarded for impact, take part in accelerated career growth, thrive with highly flexible benefits, and are empowered to do your best work in a remote-first environment. In alignment with our overall Total Rewards Philosophy, we believe compensation should be fair, clear, consistent, and aligned to growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Italy Base Hiring Range:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€50.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€70.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Black Duck Software, Inc. helps organizations build secure, high-quality software, minimizing risks while maximizing speed and productivity. Black Duck, a recognized pioneer in application security, provides SAST, SCA, and DAST solutions that enable teams to quickly find and fix vulnerabilities and defects in proprietary code, open source components, and application behavior. With a combination of industry-leading tools, services, and expertise, only Black Duck helps organizations maximize security and quality in DevSecOps and throughout the software development life cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Field Chief Technology Officer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: EMEA, Remote (Black Duck has entities in UK, Germany, Netherlands, France, Italy, Ireland, Finland, Sweden)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Duck® meets the board-level risks of modern software with True Scale Application Security, ensuring uncompromised trust in software for the regulated, AI-powered world. Only Black Duck solutions free organizations from tradeoffs between speed, accuracy, and compliance at scale while eliminating security, regulatory, and licensing risks. Whether in the cloud or on premises, Black Duck is the only choice for securing mission-critical software everywhere code happens. With Black Duck, security leaders can make smarter decisions and unleash business innovation with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Regional Field Chief Technology Officer to serve as a senior technical executive, trusted advisor, and public voice of our technology strategy in the market. In this role, the Regional Field CTO will operate at the intersection of technology, sales, and the customer — engaging directly with C-level and technical leaders at our most strategic customer accounts, translating our AI-driven platform capabilities into credible technical narratives, and representing the company as a thought leader across the industry. This is a customer-facing, pre-sales technical leadership role reporting to the VP of Sales Engineering, with a dotted line to Product &amp;amp; Technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as trusted technical advisor and recurring executive sponsor for C-level and senior technical stakeholders at strategic, enterprise, federal and other key accounts — pivoting fluidly between business strategy conversations, risk, compliance, and deep technical architecture reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead highly visible, multidisciplinary technical engagements of strategic importance across the region, including executive briefings, architecture reviews, whiteboard sessions, customer advisory feedback loops, and partner or analyst-facing discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Black Duck as a technical evangelist for the platform and roadmap within a region, delivering keynotes, webinars, whitepapers, and thought leadership content at industry events, and representing the company externally with press, analysts, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Black Duck platform AI/ML, detection engine, and platform architecture capabilities into clear, credible narratives for both technical and executive audiences, speaking candidly to responsible AI practices such as data privacy, model governance, and human-in-the-loop controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Presales leadership on the region’s most strategic and enterprise opportunities, leading technical deep-dives, architecture reviews, whiteboard sessions, and executive briefings, and advising on the technical implications of new product launches, roadmap changes, and competitive positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RFPs and security questionnaires with authoritative technical input, and articulate competitive and technical differentiation, including nuanced comparisons of AI/ML capabilities against alternatives in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively engage strategic accounts to strengthen technical trust, identify expansion opportunities, mitigate renewal risk, and guide customers toward secure software development and application security maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and solve problems of strategic or industry scope, using innovative approaches to remove technical barriers, strengthen customer confidence, and improve business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide field-informed guidance on emerging AI-assisted software development, agentic workflows, application security trends, and competitive market dynamics that may influence Black Duck strategy or customer adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture, synthesize, and escalate regional customer, partner, and market feedback into actionable input for Product, Engineering, and Sales systematically capturing technical objections and influencing the roadmap, packaging, launch readiness, and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, enable, and review technical storytelling by sales engineers and account executives, including how to explain AI features accurately without overclaiming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in a senior technical leadership role (CTO, Sales Engineering leader, Principal Architect, or equivalent), including several years in a customer-facing or field/pre-sales capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record engaging and influencing C-level and senior technical audiences at enterprise organizations, with demonstrated success across complex enterprise sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in application security (SAST, SCA, DAST), enterprise architecture, cloud/SaaS platforms, APIs and integrations, and security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, practical understanding of AI/ML concepts as applied to security (e.g., anomaly detection, large language models, behavioral analytics, AI-assisted software development, agentic workflows), along with a candid grasp of their limitations and the practical limitations and controls needed for responsible adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success negotiating with and influencing executive leadership, significant customers, partners, analysts, or vendors to shape technical decisions and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise wide latitude in determining objectives and approaches for complex, critical assignments with material regional, functional, or market impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping standards, methods, practices, or market-facing technical narratives within an industry or discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate complex technical concepts into clear stories for both executive and highly technical audiences, including customers, partners, press, analysts, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated industry presence — conference speaking, published thought leadership, active contribution to industry/analyst communities, customer advisory leadership, or comparable external technical influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, able to translate complex technical concepts for both technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel up to 50% to customer sites and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Cybersecurity, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or other advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Black Duck is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all applicants for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, sexual orientation, veteran or military service status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Black Duck complies with all applicable laws prohibiting employment discrimination in every jurisdiction where it operates and provides reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities in accordance with applicable law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;LTK’s mission is to empower the world’s premium lifestyle Creators to achieve maximum economic success. We have a huge opportunity ahead of us and we’re looking for team members who want to create, innovate and disrupt an industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We empower our team members to drive innovation, create value, and continue to spearhead the creation of this industry — a game changer when it comes to career growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Brand Partnerships (UK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London, UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; VP, Brand Partnerships (EU)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full Time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Brand Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; to join our growing EU Brand Partnerships team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior commercial role responsible for driving enterprise growth across the UK through the acquisition, growth and strategic development of LTK&#39;s most valuable brand partnerships. You&#39;ll own the development of high-value relationships with leading fashion, beauty, lifestyle and luxury brands, positioning LTK as a trusted, long-term creator commerce partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As one of the UK&#39;s most senior commercial leaders, you&#39;ll lead consultative sales conversations with executive stakeholders, identifying opportunities to solve complex marketing challenges through LTK&#39;s full-funnel creator marketing solutions. You&#39;ll be responsible for building new enterprise relationships while strategically growing a portfolio of LTK Europe’s highest-potential and highest-value brand partners. Through a consultative approach, you&#39;ll develop a healthy pipeline of opportunities, convert new business and expand long-term investment across your accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Brand Activation, Creator Success, Campaign Operations and Marketing, you&#39;ll own the long-term growth of strategic brand partners, taking over once brands have successfully onboarded and transitioned through their initial activation phase to maximise retention, investment and lifetime value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an experienced enterprise seller who thrives on opening new opportunities, influencing senior decision-makers and building meaningful commercial partnerships across every level of a brand&#39;s marketing organisation—from executive leadership through to day-to-day marketing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Sales &amp;amp; Market Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the UK enterprise &amp;amp; mid market business strategy across fashion, beauty, lifestyle and luxury sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a healthy pipeline of high-value opportunities through strategic prospecting, networking and industry engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships across senior marketing organisations, including CMOs, Marketing Directors, Digital, Social, Affiliate and Ecommerce leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex consultative sales cycles from discovery through negotiation and contract execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position LTK as a strategic creator commerce partner by delivering insight-led, value-based sales conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently exceed ambitious Managed Services and Advertising revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Account Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow a portfolio of strategic brand partners, identifying opportunities to increase investment across LTK&#39;s commercial solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop long-term account strategies that deepen relationships and expand LTK&#39;s footprint across multiple business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities across creator collaborations, paid media, content, licensing, events and emerging commercial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted executive relationships that position LTK as a long-term strategic marketing partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver executive business reviews, strategic recommendations and commercial proposals that support long-term partnership growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with clients to solve evolving marketing challenges through innovative creator-led solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Brand Activation to ensure a seamless transition of newly activated brands into long-term commercial management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing, Creator Success, Campaign Operations, Product and Operations to deliver an exceptional partner experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market intelligence and customer feedback to influence product development, commercial strategy and go-to-market initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of sales playbooks, enterprise outreach strategies and consultative selling best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging categories, market trends and whitespace opportunities to expand LTK&#39;s enterprise footprint across the UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent LTK across the UK marketing industry by building executive-level relationships, speaking at key industry events and strengthening LTK&#39;s position as the leading creator commerce platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a senior commercial leader within the UK Brand Partnerships team, shaping commercial strategy, coach consultative selling and foster a culture of high performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently exceed individual sales quotas while contributing to wider UK Business Partnerships objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data and commercial insights to continuously optimise sales strategy and pipeline health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate pipeline management, forecasting and reporting through HubSpot and internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compelling, insight-led presentations and business cases tailored to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of consumer trends, retail innovation and the evolving creator economy to identify new commercial opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years&#39; experience in enterprise sales, strategic partnerships or business development within digital marketing, media, SaaS or influencer marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently exceeding commercial targets through enterprise new business acquisition and strategic account growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultative relationship builder who earns trust quickly and is comfortable influencing senior stakeholders through insight rather than transactional selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex consultative sales cycles involving multiple stakeholders and executive decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional commercial acumen with the ability to translate market trends into compelling business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding presentation, negotiation and executive communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of influencer marketing, affiliate marketing, social commerce and the evolving creator economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable influencing cross-functional teams and collaborating across multiple business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing senior relationships across fashion, beauty, luxury and lifestyle brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly strategic while remaining hands-on and execution focused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, entrepreneurial and driven to build new commercial opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English language skills; additional European languages are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset focused on seizing opportunities and moving with urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedication to fierce prioritization and operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability to a dynamic, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset and openness to feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: #ffffff;&quot;&gt;#LI-AJ1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and private pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexible work schedule plus Summer Fridays (workday ends at 3 pm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;25 days holiday, plus an extra day for your birthday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A benefits and wellness scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Private medical care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Paid volunteering days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work anniversary celebrations, including extra annual holidays, and luxury gifting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Interesting problems to solve with an expert team at a rapid-growth retail disruptor and the largest creator marketing platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Happy Hours and team events and activities!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About LTK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Founded in 2011, LTK is the global technology platform purpose-built to empower lifestyle creators to monetize their content. The full-service platform connects brands, creators, and shoppers with a world-class shopping app and trusted tools and technology that make content instantly shoppable. Today, premium lifestyle creators in 150+ countries drive more than $3.6 billion in annual retail sales through their LTK Shop profiles. More than 20 million consumers turn to LTK Shops in the LTK shopping platform each month to find inspiration and instantly shop the styles recommended by their favorite creators. And, more than 6,000 brands partner with LTK to gain access to its global creator network for content that converts against performance-driven, cross-channel KPIs. LTK is headquartered in Dallas, TX, and currently operates on five continents.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;To empower the world’s premium lifestyle Creators to achieve maximum economic success.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Here to win&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Commit to the journey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work well&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;LTK believes diversity, equity, and inclusion are fundamental obligations that strengthen our team. We employ a diverse, multi-disciplinary team to build a meaningful company and culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are not offering new sponsorships opportunities at this time for persons requiring employment visas;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;authorization to work in the UK is a precondition of employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Any unsolicited resumes/candidate profiles submitted through our website or to personal email accounts of employees of LTK are considered the property of LTK and are not subject to payment of agency fees&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
