&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a completed degree in a STEM field, equivalent training, or relevant practical experience in software development or quality assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have solid experience in test automation and can structure it to remain maintainable, reliable, and scalable over the long term.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have practical programming experience with &lt;strong&gt;Java&lt;/strong&gt; and write readable, maintainable test code. Experience with &lt;strong&gt;Serenity BDD&lt;/strong&gt; is a plus; alternatively, you’re willing to learn it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re familiar with testing &lt;strong&gt;APIs and microservices&lt;/strong&gt; and have a good understanding of distributed backend systems and synchronous and asynchronous communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re familiar with the fundamentals of event-driven architectures; ideally, you’ve already worked with &lt;strong&gt;Apache Kafka&lt;/strong&gt; or similar technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with &lt;strong&gt;CI/CD pipelines&lt;/strong&gt; and understand how automated tests are integrated into the development and delivery process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To you, quality means more than running test cases: you identify risks, question existing test coverage, and contribute ideas to improve our testing strategy and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work independently, in an organized and solution-oriented way, and enjoy learning about new technologies and subject areas.&lt;/li&gt;
